editorial_contributions.text:
This paper deals with an existence result for the following anisotropic Dirichlet problem with convection
\begin{align*}
\begin{cases} -\Delta_{p(z)} u(z)-\Delta_{q(z)}u(z) =\hat{r}(z)|D u(z)|^{\tau(z)-1}+f(z,u(z))& \text{in }\Omega,\\
u=0&\text{on }\partial\Omega, \end{cases}
\end{align*}
where \(\Omega\subseteq \mathbb{R}^N\) is a bounded domain with a \(C^2\)-boundary \(\partial\Omega\), \(q(\cdot)<p(\cdot)\), \(\Delta_{r(z)}\) is the \(r(z)\)-Laplace differential operator for \(1<r(\cdot)\) with \(r\in C(\overline{\Omega})\) and \(f\colon \Omega\times\mathbb{R} \to\mathbb{R}\) is a Carathéodory function that satisfies suitable conditions. Applying the frozen variable method along with a fixed point argument, the main result of this paper establishes that the problem has a positive smooth solution.
